`aplan roadmap` renders the plan grouped by cut (the milestone meta-tasks), with per-cut
rollups (done/total, ready, blocked) and the cut's critical path, plus the cross-cutting
tasks that belong to no cut. Hermetic and advisory (ADR-0009).

```
$ aplan roadmap
roadmap: 1 cut(s), 4 task(s), 7.0d effort

v0.1  Core  [todo]  1/3 done, 1 ready, 1 blocked, crit 5.0d, 6.0d effort
  Alpha       todo          Alpha task
  Beta        done          Beta task
  Gamma       todo          Gamma task

cross-cutting (in no cut): 1.0d effort
  Xtra        todo          Cross gate

(statuses are as claimed in the plan and gated by `aplan verify` in CI)

```

`--format json` is the machine view: cuts with rollups, members (cited evidence, not
resolved), and the per-cut critical path, plus the cross-cutting tasks.

```
$ aplan roadmap --format json
{
  "cross_cutting": [
    {
      "blocked_by": [],
      "evidence": [],
      "id": "Xtra",
      "status": "todo",
      "title": "Cross gate"
    }
  ],
  "cross_cutting_done_effort_days": 0.0,
  "cross_cutting_effort_days": 1.0,
  "cross_cutting_weeks": null,
  "cross_cutting_weeks_remaining": null,
  "cuts": [
    {
      "blocked": 1,
      "closes": [],
      "critical_path": [
        "Alpha",
        "Gamma"
      ],
      "critical_path_days": 5.0,
      "done": 1,
      "done_effort_days": 1.0,
      "effort_days": 6.0,
      "groups": [],
      "members": [
        {
          "blocked_by": [],
          "evidence": [],
          "id": "Alpha",
          "status": "todo",
          "title": "Alpha task"
        },
        {
          "blocked_by": [],
          "evidence": [
            "commit:abc1234"
          ],
          "id": "Beta",
          "status": "done",
          "title": "Beta task"
        },
        {
          "blocked_by": [
            "Alpha"
          ],
          "evidence": [],
          "id": "Gamma",
          "status": "todo",
          "title": "Gamma task"
        }
      ],
      "milestone": "M-v0.1",
      "ready": 1,
      "release": false,
      "status": "todo",
      "title": "Core",
      "total": 3,
      "version": "v0.1",
      "weeks": null,
      "weeks_remaining": null
    }
  ],
  "effort_days_per_week": null,
  "schema": "aplan/roadmap/v1",
  "total_effort_days": 7.0
}

```

`--format markdown` is the committed `ROADMAP.status.md` companion: non-aligned tables so a
content change never re-pads a neighbouring cell, and a banner plus a `verify` footer.

```
$ aplan roadmap --format markdown
<!-- generated by `aplan roadmap --format markdown`; do not edit. -->
<!-- regenerate: `aplan roadmap --format markdown` -->

# Roadmap

## Cuts

| cut | status | done/total | ready | blocked | effort | critical path |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| v0.1 | todo | 1/3 | 1 | 1 | 6.0d | 5.0d |

## v0.1 Core

| task | title | status | blocked_by | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Alpha | Alpha task | todo | - | - |
| Beta | Beta task | done | - | commit:abc1234 |
| Gamma | Gamma task | todo | Alpha | - |

## Cross-cutting (in no cut)

1.0d effort, held by tasks in no cut and not counted in the table above.

| task | title | status | blocked_by | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Xtra | Cross gate | todo | - | - |

> Statuses are as claimed in the plan and gated by `aplan verify` in CI.

```

The diagnostic formats do not apply to a rendered view; they are rejected, not collapsed:

```
$ aplan roadmap --format github
? 2
aplan: `aplan roadmap` renders a document, so it takes --format `human`, `json` or `markdown`, not `github`; `github` renders a set of findings, which `check` and `verify` do

```
